// "Draw N" ([CR#121.1]): the imperative YOU-form draw — you draw N cards, ONE
// AT A TIME ([CR#121.2] — a per-card SEQUENCE, NOT a simultaneous batch like
// mill). A SLICE-family keyword action: a `Batch(N, ...)` over the per-unit
// `Composite` named "Draw" whose body DESCRIBES the top-of-library → Hand
// relocation (an `Each` over `TopOfLibrary`, `whose` defaulting You). The
// `Batch` gives a count-doubling replacement (Alhammarret's Archive,
// [CR#121.2a,616.1g]) ONE aggregate window; the engine then runs the N
// contained draws SEQUENTIALLY — each binds the library top LATE and
// empty-checks BEFORE its move (an empty library loses the game,
// [CR#120.3,104.3c] — an executing body would silently no-op and MISS that
// loss; the stored body is the render/re-emit facet). The declarative-subject
// form ("Target player draws N cards.") is the `Draws(who, n)` macro; this is
// the bare you-imperative.
//
// Usage: Draw(1) -> "Draw a card." / Draw(3) -> "Draw three cards."
(
    name: "Draw",
    template: "draw ${0:card|cards}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect, KeywordAction],
    params: [Count],
    body: Batch(Param(0), Composite(
        name: Draw,
        body: Each(binder: Existing(TopOfLibrary(count: 1)), effect: Move(It, Hand)),
    )),
)
